  "reported_status": "Source-reported mathematical arguments only. Intake checked byte preservation and repository structure; no independent proof reconstruction, scientific-code replay, citation verification, formal proof, quantum circuit execution, or experimental validation was performed. External correctness and historical priority remain UNKNOWN. 154 reported exact supporting records and four synthetic local floating-point spectral states; unsuccessful repair runs retained; zero full-rounding runs or intake scientific replay.",
  "scientific_scope_status": "For a nonempty Boolean polytope P subset[0,1]^n, supplied integer1<=k<=n bounding support of every actual edge, rational x in P and rational A with column Euclidean norms<=1, an exact strong linear-optimization oracle returns an exactly optimizing Boolean vertex for every rational objective. The source proposes deterministic polynomial-bit construction of r<=dim F(x)+1<=n+1 Boolean vertices in the minimal ORIGINAL face F(x), with rational probabilities, exact mean x and discrepancy strictly<B(k)=16 floor(sqrt(64k))^2+136k+1<=1161k on every supported atom. Every oracle call/objective bit length and geometric reduction is charged. For each rational cost c a favorable good vertex satisfies c^T v<=c^T x; this is not cost-favorability of every atom for every c. Arbitrary matroid bases need only an independence oracle and have B(2)=2209. Singleton/integral x is immediate. The sharper N749 existence bound54k (matroid108) is not constructed here.",
